tasks.details:
This task addresses a critical power management failure where the device becomes unresponsive after extended sleep periods. The issue stems from GPIO wake configuration loss during light sleep mode on ESP32-S3.

**Root Cause Analysis**:
- GPIO module powers down during extended light sleep without proper RTC peripheral retention
- Current gpio_wakeup_enable() implementation has known issues with ESP32-S3 Arduino Core 3.2.0
- Wake sources (touch GPIO11, encoder GPIO17/18) lose configuration after ~1 hour
- Missing critical power domain configuration: esp_sleep_pd_config(ESP_PD_DOMAIN_RTC_PERIPH, ESP_PD_OPTION_ON)

**Implementation Strategy - Option A (Fix Light Sleep)**:
```cpp
// In SleepState.cpp setupLightSleep()
void setupLightSleep() {
    // Keep RTC peripherals powered during sleep
    esp_sleep_pd_config(ESP_PD_DOMAIN_RTC_PERIPH, ESP_PD_OPTION_ON);
    esp_sleep_pd_config(ESP_PD_DOMAIN_RTC_FAST_MEM, ESP_PD_OPTION_ON);

    // Configure touch wake using RTC GPIO
    rtc_gpio_init(GPIO_NUM_11);  // Touch sensor
    rtc_gpio_set_direction(GPIO_NUM_11, RTC_GPIO_MODE_INPUT_ONLY);
    rtc_gpio_wakeup_enable(GPIO_NUM_11, GPIO_INTR_LOW_LEVEL);

    // Configure encoder wake using RTC GPIO
    rtc_gpio_init(GPIO_NUM_17);  // Encoder A
    rtc_gpio_init(GPIO_NUM_18);  // Encoder B
    rtc_gpio_pullup_en(GPIO_NUM_17);
    rtc_gpio_pullup_en(GPIO_NUM_18);
    rtc_gpio_wakeup_enable(GPIO_NUM_17, GPIO_INTR_LOW_LEVEL);
    rtc_gpio_wakeup_enable(GPIO_NUM_18, GPIO_INTR_LOW_LEVEL);

    // Disable automatic GPIO sleep selection
    gpio_sleep_sel_dis(GPIO_NUM_11);
    gpio_sleep_sel_dis(GPIO_NUM_17);
    gpio_sleep_sel_dis(GPIO_NUM_18);

    // Enable touch and GPIO wake
    esp_sleep_enable_touchpad_wakeup();
    esp_sleep_enable_gpio_wakeup();
}
```

**Implementation Strategy - Option B (Switch to Deep Sleep - RECOMMENDED)**:
```cpp
// In SleepState.cpp - Replace light sleep with deep sleep
void enterInactivitySleep() {
    Serial.println("Entering deep sleep for inactivity...");

    // Save state to RTC memory
    RTC_DATA_ATTR static uint32_t sleepCounter = 0;
    sleepCounter++;

    // Configure ext0 wake on touch (GPIO11)
    esp_sleep_enable_ext0_wakeup(GPIO_NUM_11, 0);  // Wake on LOW

    // Configure ext1 wake on encoder (GPIO17/18)
    uint64_t ext1_mask = (1ULL << GPIO_NUM_17) | (1ULL << GPIO_NUM_18);
    esp_sleep_enable_ext1_wakeup(ext1_mask, ESP_EXT1_WAKEUP_ANY_LOW);

    // Enable fast boot for quicker wake
    esp_sleep_pd_config(ESP_PD_DOMAIN_RTC_FAST_MEM, ESP_PD_OPTION_ON);

    // Enter deep sleep
    esp_deep_sleep_start();
}

// In firmware.ino setup()
void handleWakeupReason() {
    esp_sleep_wakeup_cause_t wakeup_reason = esp_sleep_get_wakeup_cause();

    switch(wakeup_reason) {
        case ESP_SLEEP_WAKEUP_EXT0:
            Serial.println("Wakeup from touch");
            stateMachine.resumeFromSleep();
            break;
        case ESP_SLEEP_WAKEUP_EXT1:
            Serial.println("Wakeup from encoder");
            stateMachine.resumeFromSleep();
            break;
        default:
            Serial.println("Normal boot");
            break;
    }
}
```

**StateMachine Integration**:
```cpp
// Modify StateMachine.cpp inactivity handling
void StateMachine::checkInactivity() {
    if (currentState != &idleState) return;

    unsigned long currentTime = millis();
    if (currentTime - lastActivityTime > INACTIVITY_TIMEOUT) {
        Serial.println("Inactivity timeout - entering deep sleep");

        // Save current state if needed
        preferences.putUInt("lastState", STATE_IDLE);
        preferences.putUInt("lastProject", currentProjectIndex);

        // Transition to sleep
        sleepState.enterInactivitySleep();  // This will reset device
    }
}
```

**Additional Considerations**:
1. Update INACTIVITY_TIMEOUT to 180000 (3 minutes) in Constants.h
2. Implement state persistence using Preferences library for seamless wake experience
3. Consider adding visual/LED indication before entering deep sleep
4. Test with external button (GPIO19) wake source for consistency with Task 12
5. Monitor power consumption to verify deep sleep achieves <10mA current draw
